ators in planar $ \\mathcal{N} $ = 4 supersymmetric Yang-Mills (SYM). We conjecture that all loop corrections derive from an integrand which enjoys a ten-dimensional symmetry. This symmetry combines spacetime and R-charge transformations. By considering a 10D light-like limit, we extend the correlator/amplitude duality by equating large R-charge octagons with Coulomb branch scattering amplitudes. Using results from integrability, this predicts new finite amplitudes as well as some Feynman integrals.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"Springer"}},{"source":"arXiv","value":"We consider four-point correlation functions of protected single-trace scalar operators in planar $N$ = 4 supersymmetric Yang-Mills (SYM). We conjecture that all loop corrections derive from an integrand which enjoys a ten-dimensional symmetry. This symmetry combines spacetime and R-charge transformations. By considering a 10D light-like limit, we extend the correlator/amplitude duality by equating large R-charge octagons with Coulomb branch scattering amplitudes. Using results from integrability, this predicts new finite amplitudes as well as some Feynman integrals.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"control_number":1867510,"dois":[{"source":"Springer","value":"10.1007/JHEP03(2022)151"},{"material":"publication","source":"arXiv","value":"10.1007/JHEP03(2022)151"}],"preprint_date":"2021-06-07","arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["hep-th"],"value":"2106.03892"}],"titles":[{"source":"Springer","title":"Ten dimensional symmetry of $ \\mathcal{N} $ = 4 SYM correlators"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"Ten dimensional symmetry of $N$ = 4 SYM correlators"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"Ten dimensional symmetry of N=4 SYM correlators"}],"document_type":["article"]},"id":"1867510","links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1867510?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1867510?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1867510?format=latex-